{#- console-header.njk — ONE header for both consoles

   There were two, and they drifted: the staff one grew a link to the admin
   area, the admin one grew a way back, and neither could describe somebody who
   belonged in both. This renders BOTH rows and lets the account decide which
   it gets — one row for most people, two for somebody who is genuinely both.

   EVERY LINK IS RENDERED AND THEN HIDDEN, rather than rendered conditionally.
   The pages are static: Eleventy does not know who is asking, and building a
   variant per role would mean shipping the whole console several times over.
   So the roles ride along in `data-roles` and staff.js removes what does not
   apply, from an identity it already has cached before first paint.

   WHICH MEANS THIS IS NOT A SECURITY BOUNDARY, and nothing here should ever be
   mistaken for one. Every endpoint checks the role itself. A hidden link is a
   tidier console, not a closed door. -#}

<header class="console" id="console">
  <div class="console-in">

    {#- The wordmark is a link to whichever console the person actually has.
       It used to be hardcoded to /staff/, which sent a board member to a page
       that refused them the moment they clicked their own logo. -#}
    <a class="mark console-mark" id="consoleHome" href="/staff/" aria-label="Thauma">{% set logoId = "console" %}{% include "brand/logo.njk" %}</a>

    {#- THE BELL (0060; Chase 2026-10-13: "Add the in app notifications
       bell"). The notices email also sends (workers/src/lib/notify.js), kept
       here, unread until the list is opened. Outside the folding menu so a
       phone shows it beside Menu; on a wide screen it sits before the public
       site and your name (staff.css `order`). Filled by staff.js. -#}
    <div class="console-bell" id="consoleBell">
      <button type="button" class="console-bell-btn" id="consoleBellBtn"
              aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="consoleBellMenu"
              data-i18n-attr="aria-label:bell.title,title:bell.title" aria-label="Notifications" title="Notifications">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
             stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <path d="M6 16V11a6 6 0 0 1 12 0v5l1.5 2h-15z"/><path d="M10 20.5a2 2 0 0 0 4 0"/>
        </svg>
        <span class="console-bell-n" id="consoleBellN" hidden></span>
      </button>
      {#- Unread and recently read; Clear (one, or all) moves a notice to Past,
          and so do six hours after reading it (0061) — Past keeps a year. -#}
      <div class="console-bell-menu" id="consoleBellMenu">
        <div class="console-bell-head">
          <button type="button" class="console-bell-back" id="consoleBellBack" hidden>
            <span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span> <span data-i18n="bell.back">Back</span></button>
          <span id="consoleBellTitle" data-i18n="bell.title">Notifications</span>
          <button type="button" class="console-bell-act" id="consoleBellClearAll" data-i18n="bell.clearAll" hidden>Clear all</button>
        </div>
        <ol class="console-bell-items" id="consoleBellItems"></ol>
        <div class="console-bell-foot">
          <button type="button" class="console-bell-act" id="consoleBellPast" data-i18n="bell.past">Past Notifications</button>
          <a href="/staff/settings/#notifications" data-i18n="bell.settings">Choose what arrives</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {#- ONE BUTTON ON A PHONE (mockup board 1). Two rows of links do not fit
       390px — five of the eight staff links were off the edge — so on a
       narrow screen the rows and the actions fold behind this, and open as a
       list. On a wide screen it is not shown. -#}
    <button type="button" class="ghost-btn console-menu-btn" id="consoleMenuBtn"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="consoleMenu">
      <span class="when-closed" data-i18n="nav.menu">Menu</span>
      <span class="when-open" data-i18n="nav.close">Close</span>
    </button>

    <div class="console-menu" id="consoleMenu">
    <div class="console-rows">
      {%- for area in ["staff", "admin"] %}
      {%- set list = consoleNav.row.staff if area == "staff" else consoleNav.row.admin %}
      {%- set current = staffPage if area == "staff" else adminPage %}
      {#- The roles are BOTH a class and an attribute. The class is what CSS
         matches, so the right rows are there in the first paint; the attribute
         is what staff.js reads afterwards. Same list, two readers. -#}
      <div class="console-row r-{{ consoleNav.rows[area] | join(' r-') }}"
           data-row="{{ area }}"
           data-roles="{{ consoleNav.rows[area] | join(' ') }}">
        <span class="console-badge is-{{ area }}"
              data-i18n="nav.badge.{{ area }}">{{ "Staff" if area == "staff" else "Administration" }}</span>
        <nav>
          {%- for p in list %}
          <a href="{{ p.url }}" class="r-{{ p.roles | join(' r-') }}"
             data-roles="{{ p.roles | join(' ') }}"
             {% if p.slug == current %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
             data-i18n="{{ ('nav.' + ('home' if p.slug == 'index' else p.slug)) if area == 'staff' else ('adm.nav.' + p.slug) }}">{{ p.label }}</a>
          {%- endfor %}
        </nav>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    {#- YOU: your name opens what is about you — the sites, Settings, your
       Activity, What's new, Sign out (mockup board 1). Sign out used to sit
       beside the navigation as the loudest button in the header, which is the
       wrong thing to be loudest.

       THE SITES MOVED IN HERE (2026-10-13, Chase: "The nav doesn't fit
       anymore in the header … the header needs a redesign again so that
       everything fits well"). With the bell, "Your site ↗" and "Public
       site ↗" beside the name took about 290px from the two rows, and the
       staff row ran under the bell ("Site Cr…"). The header is now the mark,
       the rows, the bell and your name; the two ways out of the console are
       the first lines under your name. -#}
    <div class="console-actions">
      <div class="console-me">
        <button type="button" class="console-me-btn" id="consoleMeBtn"
                aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="consoleMe">
          <span class="pill" id="partnerPill" hidden></span>
          <span class="console-me-fallback" data-i18n="nav.account">Account</span>
          <span class="console-caret" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="console-me-menu" id="consoleMe">
          {#- The ministry's own site, once it is switched on (0044) — filled
              and shown by staff.js from /api/staff-site?brief. Beside it,
              Thauma's own site steps aside for anyone who does not look
              after it — partners and staff want their ministry's site, and
              two "site ↗" lines read as the same link twice. Administrators
              and communications keep both (staff.css). -#}
          <a class="console-site area-mysite" id="consoleMySite" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener" hidden>
            <span data-i18n="nav.mySite">Your Site</span> <span class="area-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
          <a class="console-site area-public" href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <span data-i18n="nav.viewSite">Public Site</span> <span class="area-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
          {%- for p in consoleNav.menu %}
          <a href="{{ p.url }}" class="r-{{ p.roles | join(' r-') }}"
             data-roles="{{ p.roles | join(' ') }}"
             {% if p.slug == staffPage %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
             data-i18n="nav.{{ p.slug }}">{{ p.label }}</a>
          {%- endfor %}
          <a href="/cdn-cgi/access/logout" class="console-signout" data-i18n="nav.signout">Sign Out</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</header>

{#- A PAGE OPENS AT ONCE, AGAIN AND AGAIN (Chase, 2026-10-20: "once this
   Website page opens the first time, if you navigated away to People and
   back to Website, Website should open quickly again. Right now, it reloads
   every time"). A link in the header held for a moment (hover, or a press
   on a phone) has its page drawn behind the one on screen — its words, its
   data, its preview — so the click shows a page already loaded, where the
   browser can (Chrome and Edge). Not the page you are on, and not a link
   to another site. Loading a console page only reads; nothing it does on
   arrival changes anything, which is what makes drawing it early safe —
   keep it so. -#}
<script type="speculationrules">{"prerender":[{"where":{"and":[{"selector_matches":".console-row nav a, .web-areas a"},{"not":{"selector_matches":"[aria-current]"}}]},"eagerness":"moderate"}]}</script>
